From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: Keep LDAC when A2DP is encoded in software

A2dpCodecs::init() disables the LDAC source codec unless the Bluetooth
SoC reports split A2DP LDAC support. That only matters on the offload
path, where the SoC encodes: with A2DP offload off the stack encodes
LDAC itself with libldacBT, which is linked in either way. Phones whose
SoC can't encode LDAC and that run A2DP in software lost LDAC for
nothing.

Only ask the SoC when A2DP offload is enabled, read the same way as
isA2DPOffloadEnabled(): ro.bluetooth.a2dp_offload.supported and not
persist.bluetooth.a2dp_offload.disabled.

Change-Id: I32eed4050cdb824c41fad4dd997359ef4fc7ca16
---
 system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_codec_config.cc | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_codec_config.cc b/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_codec_config.cc
index a0eaca3245..b7c1c09def 100644
--- a/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_codec_config.cc
+++ b/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_codec_config.cc
@@ -720,7 +720,13 @@ bool A2dpCodecs::init() {
       log::info("LHDCv5 codec disabled");
     }
 
-    if(codec_index == BTAV_A2DP_CODEC_INDEX_SOURCE_LDAC) {
+    // The SoC only has to encode LDAC on the split (offload) path. With
+    // A2DP offload off the stack encodes it in software with libldacBT, so
+    // keep LDAC even when the SoC cannot encode it.
+    bool a2dp_offload =
+            osi_property_get_bool("ro.bluetooth.a2dp_offload.supported", false) &&
+            !osi_property_get_bool("persist.bluetooth.a2dp_offload.disabled", false);
+    if (codec_index == BTAV_A2DP_CODEC_INDEX_SOURCE_LDAC && a2dp_offload) {
       log::verbose("codec_index is BTAV_A2DP_CODEC_INDEX_SOURCE_LDAC");
       uint8_t soc_add_on_features_len = 0;
       const bt_device_soc_add_on_features_t* soc_add_on_features =
-- 
